<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
        <title>IT Archive | Sombra Technologies</title>

        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/app.css" />

        <style>
            .archive-document {
                max-width: 900px;
                margin: 50px auto;
                padding: 45px;
                background: #fff;
                color: #252936;
                box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
                font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            }

            .document-header {
                border-bottom: 3px solid #7028a5;
                padding-bottom: 20px;
                margin-bottom: 30px;
            }

            .company-name {
                color: #7028a5;
                font-size: 13px;
                font-weight: bold;
                letter-spacing: 3px;
                text-transform: uppercase;
            }

            .document-title {
                font-size: 28px;
                margin: 15px 0 5px;
            }

            .document-subtitle {
                color: #737987;
                font-size: 14px;
            }

            .metadata {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
                gap: 15px;
                background: #f4f2f7;
                padding: 20px;
                margin: 25px 0;
                font-size: 13px;
            }

            .metadata strong {
                display: block;
                color: #7028a5;
                margin-bottom: 5px;
            }

            .document-section {
                margin: 30px 0;
            }

            .document-section h2 {
                font-size: 17px;
                color: #7028a5;
                border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
                padding-bottom: 8px;
            }

            .document-section p,
            .document-section li {
                font-size: 14px;
                line-height: 1.8;
            }

            .system-table {
                width: 100%;
                border-collapse: collapse;
                margin: 15px 0;
                font-size: 13px;
            }

            .system-table th,
            .system-table td {
                padding: 12px;
                border: 1px solid #ddd;
                text-align: left;
            }

            .system-table th {
                background: #f4f2f7;
            }

            .status-warning {
                color: #b56a00;
                font-weight: bold;
            }

            .status-retired {
                color: #16834b;
                font-weight: bold;
            }

            .internal-note {
                background: #fff6e5;
                border-left: 4px solid #e3a52e;
                padding: 15px;
                margin: 20px 0;
                font-size: 13px;
            }

            .document-footer {
                border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
                margin-top: 40px;
                padding-top: 15px;
                color: #888;
                font-size: 11px;
                display: flex;
                justify-content: space-between;
            }

            .classification {
                color: #a33;
                font-weight: bold;
                letter-spacing: 1px;
            }

            .archive-stamp {
                display: inline-block;
                border: 2px solid #7028a5;
                color: #7028a5;
                padding: 6px 14px;
                transform: rotate(-4deg);
                font-weight: bold;
                font-size: 12px;
                margin-top: 15px;
            }

            @media (max-width: 650px) {
                .archive-document {
                    margin: 15px;
                    padding: 22px;
                }

                .metadata {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                }
            }
        </style>
    </head>

    <body style="background: #17151d">
        <main class="archive-document">
            <header class="document-header">
                <div class="company-name">Sombra Technologies</div>

                <h1 class="document-title">
                    Infrastructure Retirement & Access Review
                </h1>

                <div class="document-subtitle">
                    Information Technology Department · Archived Infrastructure
                    Records
                </div>

                <div class="archive-stamp">ARCHIVED COPY</div>
            </header>

            <section class="metadata">
                <div>
                    <strong>DOCUMENT ID</strong>
                    IT-2024-0918
                </div>

                <div>
                    <strong>ORIGINAL DATE</strong>
                    September 18, 2024
                </div>

                <div>
                    <strong>DEPARTMENT</strong>
                    Information Technology
                </div>

                <div>
                    <strong>DOCUMENT OWNER</strong>
                    Infrastructure Operations
                </div>

                <div>
                    <strong>CLASSIFICATION</strong>
                    Internal Use Only
                </div>

                <div>
                    <strong>LAST ARCHIVED</strong>
                    October 02, 2024
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="document-section">
                <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>

                <p>
                    This report documents the retirement of legacy
                    infrastructure services following the migration of Sombra
                    Technologies' internal employee portal to the current
                    production environment.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The migration included the removal of legacy authentication
                    services, archival storage, and several automated
                    maintenance processes. Most services were successfully
                    decommissioned. A small number of cleanup tasks remained
                    open at the time of this report.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="document-section">
                <h2>2. Legacy Service Accounts</h2>

                <p>
                    The following service identities were reviewed as part of
                    the infrastructure retirement process.
                </p>

                <table class="system-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Service Identity</th>
                            <th>Purpose</th>
                            <th>Retirement Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>svc_portal_old</td>
                            <td>Legacy portal authentication</td>
                            <td class="status-retired">Disabled</td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td>svc_archive</td>
                            <td>Historical document archive</td>
                            <td class="status-warning">Review Required</td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td>svc_backup_legacy</td>
                            <td>Automated backup rotation</td>
                            <td class="status-retired">Disabled</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <div class="internal-note">
                    <strong>Outstanding Action:</strong>
                    The svc_archive identity was scheduled for retirement after
                    the final validation of historical document access. The
                    associated cleanup task was not marked complete.
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="document-section">
                <h2>3. Authentication Review</h2>

                <p>
                    During a routine review in November 2026, the monitoring
                    team identified authentication failures associated with the
                    previously retired archive identity.
                </p>

                <table class="system-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Timestamp</th>
                            <th>Identity</th>
                            <th>Event</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>2026-11-12 02:14 UTC</td>
                            <td>svc_archive</td>
                            <td>Authentication failure</td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td>2026-11-12 02:16 UTC</td>
                            <td>svc_archive</td>
                            <td>Authentication failure</td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td>2026-11-12 02:19 UTC</td>
                            <td>svc_archive</td>
                            <td>Authentication failure</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <p>
                    The events were escalated to Infrastructure Operations. The
                    account must not be reactivated without approval.
                    Investigators should verify whether scheduled jobs or
                    archived systems still reference this identity.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="document-section">
                <h2>4. Related Support Requests</h2>

                <p>
                    The following support request was associated with the
                    archive retirement process.
                </p>

                <table class="system-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Ticket</th>
                            <th>Description</th>
                            <th>Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>ST-4930</td>
                            <td>Archive share permissions review</td>
                            <td class="status-warning">Pending Verification</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <p>
                    The ticket references the historical archive share and
                    recommends confirming that public-facing access was removed
                    after the migration.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="document-section">
                <h2>5. Migration Cleanup Notes</h2>

                <ul>
                    <li>Legacy authentication services were decommissioned.</li>
                    <li>
                        Historical documents were moved to archival storage.
                    </li>
                    <li>Old service identities were scheduled for removal.</li>
                    <li>
                        Public web-root mappings were expected to be removed
                        after validation.
                    </li>
                    <li>Final access verification remained outstanding.</li>
                </ul>

                <p>
                    The infrastructure team should verify that no historical
                    backup directories or obsolete service configurations remain
                    accessible through the employee portal.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="document-section">
                <h2>6. Report Conclusion</h2>

                <p>
                    The 2024 infrastructure migration was considered
                    operationally complete, with the exception of the
                    outstanding cleanup and access verification tasks documented
                    above.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Any unexpected activity involving retired service identities
                    should be escalated to Information Technology immediately.
                </p>
            </section>

            <footer class="document-footer">
                <span>Sombra Technologies · IT Infrastructure</span>
                <span class="classification">INTERNAL USE ONLY</span>
            </footer>
        </main>
    </body>
</html>
